Health insurance provides for payment of medical expenses in case of illness of the insure
person and his family.
It provides the following types of coverage:
Basic Medical Expenses: It covers the expenses of hospitalisation and doctor's services.
Major Medical Expenses: It covers the cost of catastrophic (sudden disaster) illness.
Long-term Hospitalisation: It covers nursing home charges for elderly people.
Medical Supplement: It fills gaps in medicare programmes of social security.
Disability Income: It replaces the income lost by the insured while the insured is unable
to work.
